Add an azd-managed model deployment before ejection.

Usage
  azd ai project deployment add [flags]

Flags
      --capacity int32  : Deployment capacity
      --force           : Replace a conflicting inline declaration
      --location string : Deployment location
      --model string    : Model name or publisher/model
      --name string     : Deployment name
      --sku string      : Deployment SKU name
      --version string  : Model version

Global Flags
  -C, --cwd string         : Sets the current working directory
      --debug              : Enables debug and diagnostics logging
  -e, --environment string : The name of the environment to use
  -h, --help               : help for add
      --no-prompt          : Runs without prompts. Uses existing values; fails if any required value or decision cannot be resolved automatically.
  -o, --output string      : The output format (supported: default, json, none) (default "default")

Examples
  Declare a managed model deployment
    azd ai project deployment add --model OpenAI/gpt-4.1 --name chat

  Apply the project's managed infrastructure
    azd provision
